Package: phwstyle
Title: Public Health Wales Corporate Styling for R Outputs
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Daryn", "Sutton", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "cheweych3w3y@gmail.com"),
    person("Canonical Ltd", role = "cph", comment = "Ubuntu font family, Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0")
  )
Description: Applies the visual identity of Public Health Wales, as used by
    its Communicable Disease Surveillance Centre, to R outputs. This is not an
    official Public Health Wales product. Provides brand colours, accessible
    and colour-blind safe palettes, colour keys that keep groups the same
    colour across reports, the Ubuntu typeface and an optional logo
    download; a 'ggplot2' theme, scales and public health charts (epidemic
    curves, population pyramids, funnel plots and statistical process
    control charts); summary, epidemiology and nested group tables rendered
    with 'flextable', 'gt', 'reactable' or Excel; themes for 'gtsummary',
    'plotly', 'DT', 'leaflet' and 'shiny'; boundaries for Welsh geographies;
    'PowerPoint' slides; R Markdown output formats (HTML, Word, PDF) and a
    Quarto extension (HTML, Word, 'Typst' PDF, 'revealjs' slides and
    dashboards).
